  description="Snapy understands your screen: say “click the second video”, “type hello in the search box” or “what’s on my screen?”. It reads Windows accessibility data first, then on-device text recognition and vision — and asks before anything irreversible."
  crumb="Screen control"
  path="/features/screen-control/"
  eyebrow="Screen control"
  title="It uses your screen the way you do."
  lead="Tell Snapy what to click or type and it finds it — buttons, links, search boxes, video thumbnails — in Chrome, Edge and most Windows apps."
