  ]}
  faqs={[
    { q: 'Which apps does screen control work with?', a: 'Chrome, Edge, File Explorer, Settings, Office and most Windows apps expose their controls to Windows accessibility, so they work instantly. Other apps use text recognition or a vision model.' },
    { q: 'Do I need a graphics card?', a: 'No. Reading windows and text recognition run on any PC. The optional local vision model is used automatically only when your PC has a graphics card; without one you can add a cloud key or turn it on as “private but slow”.' },
    { q: 'Can it do things on its own?', a: 'Only what you ask, one step at a time, with a step limit — and it stops to ask before anything that can’t be undone.' },
  ]}
